WEBVTT

00:05.070 --> 00:06.640
Where'd you get that?

00:07.030 --> 00:09.260
Isn't that the same one Elias has?

00:09.260 --> 00:12.270
I'm holding on to it for Elias.

00:19.350 --> 00:20.250
Ruth?

00:22.080 --> 00:23.340
The sea.

00:23.340 --> 00:24.000
Sea...

00:34.350 --> 00:37.340
This all seems familiar.

00:38.070 --> 00:38.830
Huh?

00:38.830 --> 00:39.800
Stella?

00:39.800 --> 00:40.550
Where's Stella?

00:40.930 --> 00:42.230
I don't sense her nearby.

00:44.250 --> 00:45.980
Ah, you're here.

00:49.410 --> 00:51.630
It's been a while since 
I've summoned anyone.

00:51.630 --> 00:53.970
I wasn't sure I did it right.

00:54.420 --> 00:56.830
So I'm glad you made it.

00:57.910 --> 00:59.300
Who are...

00:59.300 --> 01:01.320
Hello, young lady.

01:01.320 --> 01:03.240
My name is Rahab.

01:03.240 --> 01:06.910
Mage, sorcerer, demon of the sea...

01:06.910 --> 01:08.430
Call me whatever you'd like.

01:08.950 --> 01:11.360
Um, I had a friend with me.

01:11.360 --> 01:12.340
Don't worry.

01:12.340 --> 01:15.590
She'll merely be lost in 
the fog for a brief time.

01:18.810 --> 01:21.540
It seems to be authentic.

01:21.540 --> 01:26.510
I sensed someone else wearing 
the necktie I'd given him.

01:26.510 --> 01:28.180
I had my doubts, but...

01:29.630 --> 01:30.980
Glad to see he's doing well.

01:31.810 --> 01:34.490
And he's changed quite a bit, too.

01:37.220 --> 01:40.560
Are you Lindel-san's master, by chance?

01:40.560 --> 01:41.460
Lindel?!

01:41.460 --> 01:43.480
You've met Lindel, too?

01:43.480 --> 01:44.700
Fantastic!

01:44.700 --> 01:46.230
Is he doing well?

01:46.230 --> 01:47.240
Uh, yes.

01:47.530 --> 01:54.510
So, who might you be to Elias?

03:32.360 --> 03:33.170
Hey.

03:33.940 --> 03:36.530
I heard you've started your new life.

03:36.530 --> 03:38.520
I figured you'd have a lot of expenses,

03:38.870 --> 03:40.500
so I brought this to celebrate.

03:40.860 --> 03:42.100
Thanks.

03:42.100 --> 03:42.820
Where's Chise?

03:43.140 --> 03:44.810
She's with Stella right now.

03:45.780 --> 03:46.880
Shall I call her?

03:46.880 --> 03:47.870
No, it's fine.

03:48.560 --> 03:51.480
She needs her quality time.

03:52.020 --> 03:53.890
I see.

03:54.680 --> 03:57.210
I'm glad she's doing better.

03:57.870 --> 03:58.580
Yeah.

04:00.880 --> 04:04.960
She gave you that necktie 
for Christmas, didn't she?

04:05.470 --> 04:06.260
Yeah.

04:06.730 --> 04:07.900
Where's yours?

04:07.900 --> 04:09.240
Chise has it right now.

04:09.240 --> 04:10.780
I see, I see.

04:12.950 --> 04:17.300
I remember begging you for it way back when.

04:17.880 --> 04:22.760
I thought I wouldn't mind letting 
it go, but I couldn't do it.

04:24.450 --> 04:26.820
So why'd you give it to Chise?

04:30.480 --> 04:31.670
Um...

04:31.670 --> 04:33.920
He's teaching me magic.

04:33.920 --> 04:35.510
I'm his apprentice.

04:35.740 --> 04:38.240
You seemed a lot closer than just that.

04:38.560 --> 04:41.470
Ah, um... well...

04:41.840 --> 04:44.570
Chise's teaching him about being human.

04:44.570 --> 04:46.380
About being human?

04:46.380 --> 04:47.590
His bride.

04:49.460 --> 04:50.230
Bride?

04:54.450 --> 04:57.090
Was that his idea?

04:57.090 --> 04:58.340
Er, yes.

04:59.020 --> 05:00.980
Oh, dear...

05:03.110 --> 05:04.120
Um...

05:06.160 --> 05:09.150
Would you like to come 
inside to talk some more?

05:09.450 --> 05:13.800
I'll need to thank you for 
being his student and teacher.

05:13.800 --> 05:15.220
I'd love to.

05:15.220 --> 05:15.870
But...

05:16.350 --> 05:19.190
You needn't worry about time.

05:19.190 --> 05:21.650
That's the kind of place this is.

05:22.060 --> 05:26.410
Still, to think you're teaching him
 about being human... my goodness.

05:27.760 --> 05:29.890
May I ask your name?

05:30.350 --> 05:33.820
I'm in the mood to call 
someone by their name.

05:35.370 --> 05:37.350
Have a seat wherever you'd like.

05:37.600 --> 05:39.350
Is coffee all right?

05:39.350 --> 05:40.220
Yes.

05:58.330 --> 06:05.460
<i>Sea breeze, damp rocks, old 
wood, and the scent of fire.</i>

06:08.940 --> 06:11.320
I'm sorry, I don't have any milk.

06:11.320 --> 06:13.130
I'm not <i>that</i> much of a dog.

06:13.130 --> 06:14.300
All right.

06:21.780 --> 06:22.930
<i>It's odd...</i>

06:23.600 --> 06:25.770
<i>I'm sure this is our first 
time meeting, and yet...</i>

06:27.970 --> 06:28.890
Here you are.

06:29.310 --> 06:30.810
Thank you.

06:31.200 --> 06:33.530
Make yourself at home.

06:33.530 --> 06:37.070
Just pretend you're visiting 
your grandma way back home.

06:37.500 --> 06:38.400
Okay?

06:40.060 --> 06:41.260
You do resemble them.

06:41.260 --> 06:44.020
Resemble whom?

06:44.020 --> 06:46.070
Lindel-san and Elias.

06:47.510 --> 06:50.460
I suppose it's true that you become 
like the company you keep.

06:50.990 --> 06:54.390
Those two came here when
they were only this tall.

06:54.950 --> 06:57.410
Elias, too?

06:57.410 --> 06:58.440
Yeah.

06:58.440 --> 07:01.420
He lived here for a while.

07:01.830 --> 07:06.390
I thought he'd been traveling right 
after he parted ways with Lindel-san.

07:07.230 --> 07:11.700
This place is disconnected from 
everywhere and everywhen.

07:11.700 --> 07:14.390
And yet, it's joined with every place.

07:14.390 --> 07:17.640
I was sure we'd meet again...

07:20.330 --> 07:21.400
<i>He arrived...</i>

07:23.790 --> 07:27.330
<i>with his shoulders slouched, as though 
he'd been completely worn down.</i>

07:28.820 --> 07:30.120
Elias.

07:30.910 --> 07:33.670
I thought you were with Lindel.

07:33.670 --> 07:36.020
Teach me, Rahab...

07:36.620 --> 07:38.850
There's so much I don't know.

07:40.210 --> 07:42.690
There are too many humans.

07:42.690 --> 07:45.390
They're all the same, yet far too different.

07:45.800 --> 07:48.390
I don't know what to do.

07:49.300 --> 07:52.520
I don't know who to imitate.

07:53.740 --> 07:55.080
Elias...

07:55.520 --> 07:58.740
So I want to follow your lead.

07:58.740 --> 08:05.380
I'm certain that if I copy you, 
I'll do well among the humans.

08:11.550 --> 08:15.520
You like humans, don't you, Elias?

08:16.040 --> 08:17.490
I don't know.

08:17.490 --> 08:24.360
But something in my body is 
telling me that I want to know.

08:24.750 --> 08:25.710
I think.

08:27.140 --> 08:32.780
<i>For a few years, or maybe a few decades, 
Elias lived here and imitated me.</i>

08:33.060 --> 08:37.230
<i>The way I ate, the way I walked, the way I slept,</i>

08:37.670 --> 08:43.170
<i>the way I read, the way I plowed the fields, 
the I interacted with things...</i>

08:44.660 --> 08:47.770
But there were some things 
I couldn't let him copy.

08:49.570 --> 08:50.590
Rahab.

08:51.710 --> 08:54.500
How do you smile or get angry?

08:55.340 --> 08:57.790
Do you need muscles to do it?

08:57.790 --> 08:59.660
You don't need flesh to move.

08:59.660 --> 09:02.140
If you enjoy an experience, 
that counts as smiling.

09:02.960 --> 09:04.560
Enjoyment...

09:05.180 --> 09:07.300
What is enjoyment?

09:10.480 --> 09:15.780
<i>And one day, he left for good.</i>

09:18.800 --> 09:21.420
I haven't seen him since.

09:21.420 --> 09:23.380
I'm glad he's doing well.

09:24.080 --> 09:27.440
That's why Elias is so much like you.

09:28.800 --> 09:32.470
I couldn't even teach him to smile, though.

09:32.470 --> 09:34.380
I'm a failure as a teacher.

09:36.470 --> 09:41.340
I don't remember when,
but I taught him about family.

09:41.860 --> 09:46.550
At the time, I taught him that a family is
 a collection of people that help one another.

09:47.390 --> 09:49.260
Grandfather, grandmother.

09:49.260 --> 09:51.010
Father, mother.

09:51.010 --> 09:52.030
Child.

09:52.310 --> 09:54.640
This relationship makes them cousins.

09:55.300 --> 09:55.930
And this?

09:56.610 --> 09:58.050
A bride.

09:58.050 --> 09:59.450
A bride?

09:59.450 --> 10:02.100
What does that relationship entail?

10:03.660 --> 10:06.190
It's... someone you want to be with?

10:06.190 --> 10:08.080
Someone you want to be with?

10:08.290 --> 10:10.630
Someone you want by your side.

10:10.630 --> 10:12.970
Someone you think you should stay with.

10:12.970 --> 10:14.680
It's not just brides, either.

10:14.680 --> 10:18.600
They may be a wife, a spouse, a husband...

10:18.600 --> 10:21.050
They're a partner.

10:21.050 --> 10:22.420
A partner.

10:22.990 --> 10:25.000
Someone you want to be with.

10:25.000 --> 10:27.410
Do you mean someone to live with?

10:28.210 --> 10:30.930
That's very literal, but you could say that.

10:31.380 --> 10:33.380
Are you my bride?

10:33.380 --> 10:35.020
Most certainly not.

10:37.620 --> 10:41.130
You'll have to find a bride just for you.

10:41.130 --> 10:42.030
Got it?

10:43.790 --> 10:44.680
Okay.

10:46.040 --> 10:47.670
I mean...

10:47.900 --> 10:52.300
I tried my best to explain, I swear.

10:52.300 --> 10:53.710
I get it.

10:53.710 --> 10:56.420
I greatly appreciate your effort.

10:56.420 --> 10:57.420
Thank you.

10:58.420 --> 10:59.790
<i>I see...</i>

11:00.470 --> 11:03.050
<i>So that's what that was about.</i>

11:03.930 --> 11:05.740
You must be disappointed.

11:06.370 --> 11:11.640
His idea of a bride might be different 
from what you have in mind.

11:12.280 --> 11:15.400
If that's the case, it's my fault.

11:18.980 --> 11:23.590
When Chise was asleep with her 
injuries after fighting Joseph,

11:24.070 --> 11:26.100
I couldn't stop wondering...

11:26.100 --> 11:31.210
Why does Chise continue to act 
even when it brings her harm?

11:31.420 --> 11:32.910
You're worried.

11:33.450 --> 11:35.950
I don't want her to get hurt.

11:36.940 --> 11:41.190
At first, I was content as 
long as she didn't die.

11:41.940 --> 11:45.210
Now, even the slightest cut or 
the mildest illness upsets me.

11:47.190 --> 11:51.950
Ruth said once that nothing
 is important to Chise.

11:52.550 --> 11:56.190
That even if Chise herself values something,

11:56.190 --> 11:59.630
she doesn't expect to be 
valued the same way herself.

12:00.480 --> 12:04.620
So when she's hurt, she doesn't 
consider that someone else

12:04.620 --> 12:06.940
might also be hurt just by 
seeing her that way.

12:06.940 --> 12:09.250
Nor does she have any
 intent of sharing her pain.

12:09.790 --> 12:14.120
She believes her pain is her own to suffer.

12:15.550 --> 12:16.600
<i>So...</i>

12:17.370 --> 12:18.420
Chise.

12:19.800 --> 12:21.930
Could you wear this?

12:22.280 --> 12:23.430
This is...

12:23.430 --> 12:25.550
I can't have it break.

12:25.550 --> 12:27.250
So I'd like you to hold on to it.

12:27.990 --> 12:31.090
But if it's important to you, 
I shouldn't be the one holding onto it—

12:34.340 --> 12:37.890
You won't go getting yourself into 
trouble if you're holding this.

12:38.100 --> 12:41.280
Since you don't know how to act 
without putting yourself on the line,

12:41.280 --> 12:43.730
I want you to act in a way that 
won't allow this to be broken.

12:44.850 --> 12:47.190
It's scary when you put it that way.

12:47.190 --> 12:49.480
Good, it was supposed to be.

12:49.480 --> 12:52.600
I can't have you getting a hole
 in your stomach again.

12:53.960 --> 12:55.720
I understand.

12:55.720 --> 12:57.120
I'll hold on to it.

12:57.510 --> 12:58.940
<i>That's right.</i>

12:58.940 --> 13:01.040
<i>I can't have her break.</i>

13:02.040 --> 13:05.850
It frightens me when she 
doesn't take care of herself.

13:07.700 --> 13:08.710
What?

13:08.710 --> 13:10.090
Well.

13:10.090 --> 13:12.310
What? Why are you smirking?

13:14.010 --> 13:15.400
Bride...

13:16.160 --> 13:20.740
I'm not really functioning as one, 
so I'm not particularly disappointed.

13:20.740 --> 13:21.820
I see.

13:22.200 --> 13:26.040
Besides, whether I'm his bride or not,

13:26.040 --> 13:29.330
it doesn't change the fact
 that I'm at his side.

13:29.930 --> 13:34.360
You said you couldn't 
even teach him to smile.

13:34.360 --> 13:36.820
But Elias is definitely smiling.

13:37.180 --> 13:40.580
He might not know it himself, 
but he's smiling for sure.

13:40.580 --> 13:42.190
At least, that's what it looks like.

13:43.600 --> 13:45.360
He gets angry, too.

13:45.360 --> 13:47.320
Because you make him mad.

13:48.950 --> 13:52.640
He gets frustrated, and even jealous.

13:53.160 --> 13:59.120
I'm just guessing, but he 
seems to be giddy these days.

13:59.390 --> 14:00.590
Giddy...

14:03.010 --> 14:04.470
Really?

14:04.470 --> 14:06.240
That's what you're seeing, is it?

14:06.560 --> 14:09.590
How fortunate that he's met you.

14:10.220 --> 14:17.470
I'm not sure how to explain it, but Elias 
isn't really interested in food or his home.

14:17.860 --> 14:20.980
But he has a home he lives in.

14:21.450 --> 14:23.270
He takes care of his yard.

14:23.770 --> 14:25.750
He has a farm.

14:26.150 --> 14:28.100
And he's a proper mage.

14:28.670 --> 14:32.330
I'm certain it's all because 
he imitated you, Rahab-san.

14:34.170 --> 14:37.490
And that's the Elias who rescued me.

14:38.210 --> 14:42.480
So that was thanks to you, too.

14:43.710 --> 14:47.750
<i>The gods and the fairies 
are right there with you.</i>

14:48.100 --> 14:51.120
Even if no one will pay you any heed,

14:51.120 --> 14:54.660
even if you're sad, and distraught, and lonely,

14:54.660 --> 14:57.990
they'll always be watching over you.

14:57.990 --> 15:04.560
So have confidence and work 
on saving yourself, Elias.

15:06.410 --> 15:10.870
Thank you for helping me and Elias.

15:13.150 --> 15:19.400
You mustn't scare an old 
lady like that, Miss.

15:19.660 --> 15:22.680
I'm so glad you're Elias's partner.

15:26.700 --> 15:27.900
I'll come back.

15:28.170 --> 15:31.950
Would you mind not telling 
him that you've met me?

15:31.950 --> 15:32.850
Why not?

15:32.850 --> 15:36.250
It was out of concern, but I was 
technically surveilling him.

15:36.700 --> 15:42.390
Besides, you ought to learn how to 
handle secrets, facts, and truths.

15:42.390 --> 15:46.260
I thought mages were supposed 
to make an effort not to lie.

15:46.580 --> 15:49.390
Conceal the truth without telling lies.

15:49.390 --> 15:51.570
It's an important part of 
keeping the advantage

15:51.570 --> 15:53.510
when you're negotiating with neighbors.

15:54.050 --> 15:59.440
I can't give any more advice 
as a human, but Chise,

16:00.750 --> 16:05.720
you'll be perplexed by many things 
you can see and many you can't.

16:05.720 --> 16:09.620
You'll even have trouble 
choosing what to do.

16:09.620 --> 16:15.990
Still, I trust that our arms and 
legs will know what must be done.

16:17.710 --> 16:18.820
Chise!

16:19.380 --> 16:20.560
Stella.

16:20.560 --> 16:23.760
Did you see that crazy fog?

16:24.430 --> 16:26.070
I did.

16:27.870 --> 16:28.670
Chise?

16:57.590 --> 17:02.660
<i>No matter how many times I check, 
it's just tea imbued with magic power.</i>

17:15.190 --> 17:16.320
Elias.

17:17.060 --> 17:20.580
Are you sure you shouldn't be 
in a little more of a hurry?

17:20.580 --> 17:22.060
It'll be fine.

17:22.060 --> 17:24.590
Remember how I said I'd take a back passage?

17:24.590 --> 17:25.940
A back passage...

17:29.180 --> 17:31.260
Looks like our guide is here.

17:31.260 --> 17:33.070
Guimph?

17:35.860 --> 17:38.530
Man, I'm so late.

17:39.010 --> 17:44.010
I went back to my herd, and they wouldn't 
stop nagging me to get married and stuff.

17:46.400 --> 17:47.660
Now, then...

17:48.100 --> 17:52.130
There are back passages all over the place.

17:52.620 --> 17:55.550
An old abandoned house, a yard gate...

17:55.920 --> 17:58.800
Under a fallen tree, a cavernous root...

17:59.150 --> 18:02.850
An unused little bridge, a footpath gate...

18:02.850 --> 18:04.570
Even something like this.

18:05.790 --> 18:07.460
A phone booth.

18:08.350 --> 18:13.330
Not that I use special back 
passages very often myself.

18:13.810 --> 18:15.120
Why not?

18:18.080 --> 18:19.670
Because they aren't safe.

18:25.510 --> 18:27.280
Don't let go of my hand.

18:27.740 --> 18:30.430
There's no telling what'll 
happen if you get lost.

18:30.430 --> 18:33.830
The back passages are channels 
through this realm.

18:34.370 --> 18:38.730
Although we tend to call them back 
passages if there are no humans.

18:38.730 --> 18:41.370
This place is a bit special.

18:41.370 --> 18:44.610
Time and coordinates are quite twisted.

18:45.040 --> 18:49.000
That's why the entrance and the 
exit can be quite close together.

18:49.410 --> 18:52.320
In other words, we can travel 
in a short amount of time.

18:53.620 --> 18:58.380
So we can commute to 
the College through here?

18:58.380 --> 18:59.700
That's right.

18:59.700 --> 19:02.490
Do the other mages use it often, too?

19:02.750 --> 19:04.240
I'm not sure.

19:04.240 --> 19:06.870
I wouldn't recommend it.

19:08.160 --> 19:13.300
I have a contract with <i>them</i>, 
but it's still unpredictable.

19:13.670 --> 19:14.800
"Them"?

19:18.820 --> 19:19.850
See?

19:20.660 --> 19:23.160
They've caught our scent.

19:23.570 --> 19:25.800
These pesky guard dogs...

19:26.540 --> 19:28.890
We call them the "hound dogs."

19:30.300 --> 19:31.470
Dogs?

19:31.470 --> 19:32.510
Dogs...

19:32.510 --> 19:34.090
Hey, brothers.

19:34.090 --> 19:37.800
I have a gentleman here who wants 
to get from where we entered

19:37.800 --> 19:40.430
to where we're leaving every day.

19:40.950 --> 19:44.210
We won't make a mess, and we've 
brought payment for passage.

19:44.710 --> 19:47.120
Would you mind letting them through?

19:50.650 --> 19:51.730
What did it say?

19:51.730 --> 19:54.210
As long as we stay in this region.

19:54.210 --> 19:56.020
And go nowhere else.

20:02.370 --> 20:03.870
And if we do?

20:11.340 --> 20:13.020
We'll chase you forever.

20:11.890 --> 20:14.040
"We'll chase you forever."

20:16.410 --> 20:18.270
You heard 'em.

20:23.530 --> 20:25.340
Swallow that for me.

20:30.160 --> 20:32.760
That's the worst of it.

20:36.470 --> 20:38.440
Let's get out of here.

20:40.410 --> 20:44.810
Try to use the same entrance 
and exit as much as you can.

20:44.810 --> 20:50.860
To be honest, I don't actually know 
how much they'll tolerate, either.

21:12.360 --> 21:16.020
<i>They wouldn't stop nagging 
me to get married and stuff.</i>

21:16.450 --> 21:21.600
<i>His idea of a bride might be different 
from what you have in mind.</i>

21:22.790 --> 21:23.920
Elias.

21:26.030 --> 21:33.220
When we first met, why did you say
 you intended to make me your bride?

21:40.350 --> 21:42.650
Any changes to your health?

21:43.330 --> 21:47.160
I feel safe as long as I have 
my earmuffs and goggles.

21:47.860 --> 21:50.860
Is there anything that's been 
making you more anxious lately?

21:51.490 --> 21:53.020
Let's see...

21:53.350 --> 21:57.700
Do you know of another new student 
here named Chise Hatori?

22:08.880 --> 22:09.970
<i>No...</i>

22:11.610 --> 22:12.840
<i>No...</i>

22:14.350 --> 22:15.430
<i>No!</i>

22:16.520 --> 22:17.710
No!

22:22.350 --> 22:23.920
Awful.
